Hi everyone, Hope you all well and smiling. What an eventful few months we have had as a family! We welcomed the birth of our beautiful and now 7 week old son, Emiel Combs and now as we climb out of our cocoon and enter the world as a family of four, we are energized and ready for some drumming action! This term we are kicking off with a new rhythm in our classes along with  a new dance routine for our dancing co-op. There are some community performances coming up for all students and dancers which will be discussed in classes. Be sure to check our articles for information on Epizo Bangoura workshops coming up in November as well as festivals that you can catch a free drumming jam with us! A big thank you to Nambour Civic Centre for having us support the beautiful Grace Barbe last month and what a fantastic drumming crew that came along to see the action! Thank you! Love our drumming community! Well we look forward to seeing you in class and workshops. Yay for spring, festivals, sun and family!
